<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Act of Abjuration</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1581">1581</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Act of Abjuration was the declaration of 1581 by which the northern provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a> formally renounced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a>. It was effectively a declaration of independence during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a>. It underpinned the emergence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>, the base from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> was built.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/act-of-abjuration.jpg" alt="Act of Abjuration" width="304" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Staten-Generaal · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plakkaat_van_Verlatinghe,_pagina_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
